-- stories (3)

## First light

Before the sun clears the ridge, the valley fills with cloud. From above it looks like water that has forgotten to fall. The peaks stand out of it, pink for a minute, then white.

## The lake at midday

By noon the cloud is gone and the lake takes over. Limestone walls turn the water green-blue, and a single wooden boat is enough to give the whole frame its scale.

## After dark

When the last hut light goes off the sky shows its depth. A long exposure, a tripod on cold rock, and the galaxy lies along the ridge like a second mountain range.

This is a sample story. It shows how a longer piece reads next to its photographs.', 'https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1506905925346-21bda4d32df4?auto=format&fit=max&w=2000&q=80', 'Jagged snow peaks rising above a sea of cloud at sunrise, the sky fading from pink to blue', 2000, 1333, '#706f7b', 'alpine-light', 'alps', true, true, 1),
  ('a-slow-cup-somewhere-warm', 'A slow cup, somewhere warm', 'On choosing cafés by the table, not the menu', null, 2, 'The best cafés are decided at the table: where the light falls, whether the chair is comfortable, how long you can stay.', 'The best cafés are decided at the table: where the light falls, whether the chair is comfortable, how long you can stay.

## Look for the window

Light is the first thing worth checking. A table by the glass turns a flat white into a still life without any effort.

## Count the plants

A café with plants is a café that someone cares about. Green on the shelves, green on the counter, green leaning in from outside.

## Order slowly

The pour-over takes four minutes. That is the point.

